  "visualBrief": "Three swept corrugated roofs with raised valley sheets and sheet laps. Diagonal palm-rib panels frame the staggered rows of carved leaning posts, red iron-oxide cement sculptures, recessed scroll grille and stone forecourt relief. Painted sculpted plaster and carved posts are visible behind the central grille at close range. The elephant wing has a projecting crowned figure with extended arms above the upturned trunk and pale tusks. The left gable shelters two converging carved forearms with stacked fists and rounded finger bands. A recessed spiral waterlily sits to the left of the greeting relief. Three shallow treads rise to a recessed opening under the valley between the left and middle gables.",
  "nativeAxes": "+Z faces the forecourt, +X runs to the right wing and +Y is up.",
